WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.434
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.634
What a show tonight.

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:05.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:07.033
This is the show
to be at tonight.

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:08.601
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:10.300
Well, guys,
here's some big news.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.467
According to a new study,
dogs are more effective

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:16.100
at detecting COVID
than rapid tests.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:21.334
I'm glad we reached the point in
the pandemic where the CDC is

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:22.901
like, "I don't know, dogs?"

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:25.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:27.567
Yeah, knowing the CDC, in two
days, they're going to be like,

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:29.801
"Never mind, it's actually
rabbits. I'm sorry."

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:30.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:32.734
Seriously, I have no idea
what's going on.

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:34.968
Today, I saw Sarah McLachlan
snuggling a person

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.567
with COVID, asking pets to help.

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:37.767
I didn't know
what was happening.

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:39.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:41.300
But here's how
it works with dogs.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.334
If you have symptoms,
they sniff your crotch.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:46.100
One hump --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.667
One hump means you're negative.

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:49.067
Two humps means you're positive.

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:51.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.734
That's what they're saying.

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:56.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:56.634 --> 00:01:00.200
Yeah. Apparently, dogs are
better at detecting COVID

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.834
than rapid tests, which explains

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:03.767
now when you take
an at-home test,

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:05.701
the instructions look
a little different.

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:08.901
Yeah, now the steps are
one, open package.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:11.200
Two, remove at-home COVID test.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.400
Three, walk and feed
at-home COVID test.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.367
Four, receive unconditional love
from at-home COVID test.

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:22.267
Five, neuter at-home COVID test.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:24.501
Six, let at-home COVID test
sleep in your bed.

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:26.467
Move to couch.
That is your bed now.

00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:27.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:30.167
Seven, socialize with other
at-home COVID tests

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:31.934
at the at-home COVID test park.

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:35.067
Make small talk with other
at-home COVID test owners.

00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:38.167
Eight, repeat step 7
for 16 years.

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:39.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.234 --> 00:01:41.167
Nine, tell kids
at-home COVID test

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.968
went to live on a farm upstate.

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:44.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.000
Ten, try to get new
at-home COVID test.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.834
Eleven, discover your wife
is allergic.

00:01:49.834 --> 00:01:51.534
Twelve, get cat.

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:52.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:54.167
That's the instructions.

00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:56.868
[ Applause ]

00:01:56.868 --> 00:01:58.601
-That's a lot.

00:01:58.601 --> 00:02:01.667
-Some more news, I saw that gas
prices across the country have

00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:04.834
once again surged
to a record high.

00:02:04.834 --> 00:02:06.734
You know, at this point,
it's worth filling your car

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:08.234
with Mountain Dew and just
seeing what happens.

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:09.767
I mean, why not?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:11.033
What's the worst
that could happen?

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:12.834
I'm worried there's no solution
in sight.

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:14.200
Today, President Biden was like,

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.567
"Let's see if the COVID dogs
got anything on this."

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:18.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.868 --> 00:02:20.734
Well, guys, today was
the busiest election day

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:23.033
before November with primaries
in many states,

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:25.701
including New Jersey,
California, and Iowa.

00:02:25.701 --> 00:02:27.901
And there are a lot of races
and a lot of candidates.

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:29.467
So we thought we'd get you
caught up on what

00:02:29.467 --> 00:02:32.033
the biggest issues are to some
of the candidates right now.

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:34.934
First there's Donald Payne Jr.
of New Jersey.

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:36.100
He's running on "making it legal

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.667
to dress like
a ventriloquist dummy."

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:39.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.834
That's -- How is that --
How is that an issue?

00:02:42.834 --> 00:02:44.100
-I didn't know it was illegal.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.901
-These are issues they are
very concerned about.

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:48.534
Here's Dusty Johnson
of South Dakota.

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.300
He's running on
"changing his name to not

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.934
sound like he's
a '70s porn star."

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:53.801
[ Laughter ]
-Wow, that's his issue?

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:56.067
-Dusty -- Dusty Johnson.

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:58.601
-Dusty Johnson.

00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:01.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.734
-That's a terrible name.
-Yeah, awful name.

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:05.100
He's got a dusty johnson.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:09.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:12.667
-Then there's Mike Crispi
from New Jersey.

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:15.267
-He's running on "joining the
rebooted cast of 'Jersey Shore'

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:16.801
as their gym tan lawyer."

00:03:16.801 --> 00:03:18.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:18.334 --> 00:03:20.400
♪♪

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.133
"Your Honor."

00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:23.100
-"Tan."

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.634
-"Your Honor." Yeah.

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:27.400
Finally, there's Rick Caruso of
California.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:28.767
Higgins,
guess what he's running on.

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:30.434
-What?
-He's running on "getting people

00:03:30.434 --> 00:03:33.234
to stop saying he looks like the
villain in a '90s Disney movie

00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:35.200
where a monkey
takes over his hotel."

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:40.234
"Get that chimpanzee out of
the laundry room!"

00:03:40.234 --> 00:03:42.601
-"There is nothing
in the rule book."

00:03:42.601 --> 00:03:45.534
-Some business news --
I read that Apple is rolling out

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:50.100
their own "buy now, pay later"
service called Apple Pay Later.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.300
Trust me, you don't want to owe
money to a company that knows

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.767
your location and everything
you've ever

00:03:53.767 --> 00:03:55.701
searched for online.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:58.734
And if you miss a payment,
they send over two skinny goons

00:03:58.734 --> 00:04:00.801
from the Genius Bar named
Ethan and Zack.

00:04:00.801 --> 00:04:04.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.133
Guys, listen to this. Tom Brady
just announced that he is

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:08.467
launching his own line of Brady
brand underwear.

00:04:09.801 --> 00:04:11.901
Yep, it's the only underwear
that somehow looks better

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:13.167
after 22 years.

00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:14.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.534 --> 00:04:16.701
Meanwhile, Bill Belichick is
asking Tom

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:18.334
for some underwear or outerwear.

00:04:18.334 --> 00:04:19.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.934 --> 00:04:23.467
He'll take either one.
He'll take either one.

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:27.334
Get this. I saw that for the
summer, Panera -- I love Panera.

00:04:27.334 --> 00:04:30.000
Panera is adding lobster mac
and cheese to their menu.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.367
[ Audience oohs ]

00:04:31.367 --> 00:04:33.701
Yeah, it's actually part of
Panera's broader strategy

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:36.133
to revamp their brand,
and it really seems like

00:04:36.133 --> 00:04:37.367
they're making some big changes.

00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:38.467
Watch this commercial I saw.

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:40.734
-Introducing the all-new
Panera Bread.

00:04:40.734 --> 00:04:43.000
You've always loved our
sandwiches and delicious soups

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.334
served in bread bowls.

00:04:44.334 --> 00:04:46.968
Well, now, come and try
our lobster mac and cheese.

00:04:46.968 --> 00:04:48.501
Also served in a bread bowl.

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:51.868
Or cool off with our refreshing
lemonade, served in bread cups.

00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:54.868
Hey, how about a bread salad
or a bread cookie

00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:56.734
dunked in an ice-cold
glass of bread?

00:04:56.734 --> 00:04:58.701
Enjoy it while you sit in
our bread booth.

00:04:58.701 --> 00:05:00.667
And wave to our [Demonic voice]
bread employees

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:01.968
with your bread wife

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:05.033
and your bread kids
and your bread dog --

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:06.200
-[ Barks ]

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.801
-[ Normal voice ]
And we've got fresh bagels.

00:05:07.801 --> 00:05:09.067
Panera Bread.

00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:10.701
[ Demonic voice ] Bread!

00:05:10.701 --> 00:05:13.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:16.767
-Interesting.

00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:18.200
-Wow!

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:22.868
-I heard that a -- I heard that
a massive lettuce shortage

00:05:22.868 --> 00:05:26.267
in Australia has forced the KFC
restaurants there to put

00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:27.601
cabbage on their burgers.

00:05:27.601 --> 00:05:29.968
[ Audience groans ]
Yeah.

00:05:29.968 --> 00:05:32.234
My question is, "Who's getting
burgers at KFC?"

00:05:32.234 --> 00:05:33.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.701 --> 00:05:35.133
-Oh!

00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:37.901
Oh, switch 'em up!
Switch 'em up!

00:05:37.901 --> 00:05:40.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.033
Damn!

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:44.367
-They said the bad news is
"we're out of lettuce."

00:05:44.367 --> 00:05:45.367
And then the customer said,

00:05:45.367 --> 00:05:46.534
"Okay, then what's
the bad news?"

00:05:46.534 --> 00:05:47.634
[ Laughter ]
-Hey!

